; regression test: a bare (unkeyworded) claim can be labelled, exactly like `use`/`show`/`def`
; -- every statement, keyworded or not, is parsed through the same `check_expr_label`. `Q` is
; only ever established via the labelled bare claim "derived-q" (derived by "impl-elim" from
; `P`/`P implies Q`, never a bare `use Q`), so it has survived if `bool Q` now raises.
load load-export-bare-claim-helper
expect "EvalError"
    bool Q
true
;;; Proof checked.
